v 3
d 'APEXOG': module to estimate APE/AIE bounds in a control-function probit under plausibly-exogenous IVs (Conley, Hansen, & Rossi 2012)
d
d   apexog estimates Conley, Hansen, and Rossi's (2012)
d  "plausibly exogenous" UCI and LTZ bounds with the Average Partial
d   Effect (APE; probability scale) of an endogenous regressor in a
d   control-function probit (cfprobit) as the target functional --
d   rather than the latent-index coefficient targeted by Damian
d   Clarke's plausexog (which works on ivregress 2sls).
d
d   With aie(X Z), the target switches to the Average Interaction
d   Effect for the continuous-by-continuous interaction c.X##c.Z,
d   in the style of ginteff (Radean 2023).
d
d   Inference uses a Murphy-Topel two-step sandwich computed in
d   Mata; at gamma = 0 the resulting APE SE matches cfprobit +
d   margins, dydx() to machine precision.
d
d   Features (v0.20.0):
d     - exact probability-scale output: at every refit apexog reports the
d       exact Pr-scale value of each instrument's violation (average
d       discrete change for a 0/1 instrument, average derivative
d       otherwise, from the refitted model).  UCI: e(grid_pr), printed
d       beside each gamma range, and the graph's x-axis with gunits(pr);
d       LTZ: e(gamma_sim), e(gamma_pr_sim), exact mean/sd of the draws.
d       gunits(pr) input stays first order; no stored result of v0.19.1
d       changes.
d
d   Features (v0.19.1):
d     - documentation + header warning only (no numeric change): the
d       sigma_tilde conversion behind gunits(structural) is derived for a
d       LINEAR first stage.  With firststage(probit|fprobit|poisson) the
d       Table 1 Monte Carlos of the companion paper put the correct offset
d       at the UNSCALED structural gamma (Wald coverage at the true
d       violation 0.936 vs 0.589 for binary d and 0.950 vs 0.881 for
d       fractional d, raw gamma vs gamma/sqrt(1-rho^2); zero-bias offset
d       within 5% of the structural gamma), so gunits(structural) should
d       not be used with those first stages: the results header now prints
d       a warning line (results unchanged) and the help states the scope,
d       that e(stilde) is then not a conversion factor, and that e(stilde)
d       is a baseline-fit quantity that moves with the true violation.
d
d   Features (v0.19.0):
d     - firststage(biprobit): recursive bivariate probit engine for a
d       single 0/1 endogenous regressor (joint MLE, gamma as an offset in
d       the outcome equation, ASF discrete-change APE with an MLE
d       delta-method SE; no generated regressor).  Exact under joint
d       normality of the structural errors, where the generalized-residual
d       control function of the probit/fprobit/poisson first stages is only
d       Wooldridge's (2014, 2015) approximation: large-N bias -2.7%, -11.6%,
d       -50.6% at error correlations 0.3, 0.5, 0.8 in the validation design.
d       That caveat is now disclosed in the results header, the help file
d       (Methods, Input requirements) and the showcase.  gunits(structural)
d       is identical to the default for this engine (sigma_tilde = 1);
d       e(rho) returns the baseline error correlation.
d
d   Features (v0.18.0):
d     - input validation: 0/1 outcome check, disjoint variable lists,
d       gmin<=gmax, first-stage support checks (probit 0/1, fprobit
d       [0,1], poisson >=0), first-stage sample/control-function guards;
d       level(95) accepted alongside level(.95); vce(cl id) abbreviations
d       and string cluster ids; names unabbreviated; e(N_clust)/e(clustvar);
d       full e(cmdline); replay honours level().  Fixes: debug crash
d       (r(111)), uci+graph in AIE mode, 32-character name overflow for
d       long endog names, if/in ignored by the instrument cleaning.
d
d   Features (v0.17.0):
d     - gunits(structural): supply gamma values on the STRUCTURAL latent
d       scale (total error variance 1); they are converted to probit-index
d       units via sigma_tilde = (1 + b_cf' Var(chat) b_cf)^(-1/2) from the
d       baseline fit.  Feeding a structural-units prior unrescaled is a
d       scale miscalibration with wide-prior LTZ coverage 2*Phi(z*st)-1
d       (~0.88 instead of 0.95 at endogeneity correlation 0.6).
d       sigma_tilde always reported in the header and stored in e(stilde).
d
d   Features (v0.16.1):
d     - UCI grid guard: grid^(#instruments) above c(max_matsize) now
d       errors early with an actionable message (use ltz, fewer
d       instruments, or a coarser grid) instead of a cryptic matsize
d       failure
d
d   Features (v0.16.0):
d     - estimation command proper: posts e(b) (baseline target estimates)
d       with full cross-target Murphy-Topel e(V) and e(sample); test,
d       lincom, estimates store, and replay work
d     - LTZ delta sweep via graphomega(): bounds vs prior width, the
d       CHR (2012) Figures 1-2 display; stored in e(sweep)
d     - sample guards: missing cluster ids / any endog marked out;
d       perfect prediction and collinear CF columns caught with a
d       warning instead of silent misalignment
d
d   Features (v0.15.0):
d     - gunits(pr): supply gamma values as PROBABILITY POINTS; they are
d       converted to latent-index units via m_phi = mean(normalden(xb))
d       from the baseline fit (puts apexog on the same violation scale
d       as plausexog run on a binary outcome).  m_phi reported and
d       stored in e(mphi).
d
d   Features (v0.14.0):
d     - LTZ interval now CONVOLVES sampling noise with the gamma prior
d       (CHR 2012 eq. 7; the simulation analog of plausexog's
d       V + A*Omega*A').  The prior-only spread of point APEs is
d       still reported as a labeled sensitivity band.
d
d   Features (v0.13.x):
d     - endog-interaction AIE: (c.d c.d#c.X = Z c.Z#c.X) with
d       target(c.d#c.X) and auto cfinteract
d     - factor-variable instruments cleaned to full rank
d
d   Features (v0.12.0):
d     - RENAMED from plausexog_ape to apexog (no behavioral change)
d
d   Features (v0.11.0):
d     - target() accepts fv interaction specs for AIE:
d       target(c.X#c.Z) -> cts x cts cross-partial
d       target(c.X#i.d) -> cts x binary firstdiff
d       target(i.X#i.d) -> binary x binary 2nd discrete diff
d     - prefixes OVERRIDE value-based type auto-detection
d     - aie() retained as back-compat shorthand
d
d   Features (v0.10.0):
d     - i./c. prefix on (endog = iv) clause auto-defaults the first-stage
d       type ((c.d=z) -> linear, (i.d=z) -> probit)
d     - target() option narrows which endogenous regressor's APE is reported
d
d   Features (v0.9.0):
d     - methods: uci, ltz
d     - targets: APE (default) or AIE via aie(X Z)
d     - first stages: linear, probit, fprobit, poisson (v0.19: biprobit)
d     - 1+ endogenous regressors with multi-clause syntax
d       (d1=z1 z2)(d2=z3) for per-endog instrument sets
d     - LTZ priors: Gaussian via mu()/omega(), OR distribution()
d       (normal, uniform, chi2, t, gamma, poisson, special)
d     - vce: robust (default), cluster
d     - optional graph output for UCI bounds and LTZ histogram
d
d   Requires: Stata 18.  StataNow is NOT required: apexog implements the
d            control-function probit directly (regress/probit/fracreg/
d            poisson + Mata) and never calls cfprobit at runtime; the
d            cfprobit/cfregress comparisons live only in the validation
d            suite.
d
d Author: Jesper N. Wulff, Department of Economics and Business Economics, Aarhus University
d Support: email jwulff@econ.au.dk or https://github.com/jespernwulff/stata-apexog
